Instructions

Karo In-Kind & MoU Drafter

Evaluate in-kind barter contributions against cash floors and draft legally structured Memorandums of Understanding (MoUs) for #Karo sponsors.

When to Use

When evaluating whether free workshops, materials, or catering meet the sponsorship tier threshold.
When drafting an MoU for Title, Zone, Kit, or Workshop partners.
Core Contract Clauses to Always Include

Financial & Commercial Terms:
100% upfront payment upon signing (strictly no progress advances or post-event settlements).
In-kind valuation breakdown: List itemized goods/services and agreed market value.
Production Safeguards:
Branding lock: Logos are not sent for merchandise printing (aprons, stirrers, banners) until cash has cleared.
In-Kind Delivery Deadline: Physical goods or materials must arrive at the Pune storage site by November 30, 2026.
Charity Alignment:
Explicit declaration that net event proceeds support the Cuddles Foundation.
Deliverable Scope:
Itemized list of on-ground branding, Passport zone challenge rules, and macro content deliverables.
